# Story 4.5 (FR50) — error-contract gate allowlist.
#
# Files listed here (relative to api/) are exempt from the
# "no `catch (...) { ... new JsonResponse(...) }` in controllers" gate.
# Controllers MUST not catch-and-respond — they should throw a DomainException
# instead and let the ExceptionResponder listener build the RFC 9457 Problem
# Details body. See docs/api-error-contract.md#how-to-add-a-new-error.
#
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored. Paths must be POSIX,
# relative to api/, with no leading slash.
#
# Adding a new entry here is a deliberate exception and SHOULD be reviewed:
# the only legitimate reasons are
#   (a) the file is part of the error-contract plumbing itself
#       (e.g. ExceptionResponder, ProblemDetailsResponder), OR
#   (b) the file is legacy controller code whose migration to the new
#       error contract is tracked by a follow-up story.
#
# Story 4.5 ships with (b)-only entries — the Bank controllers predate the
# error-contract migration and are scheduled to move off catch-and-respond
# in a follow-up. Once migrated, remove the corresponding line.

